# Design system: form controls, fields and search compose their primitives; client-side search
# has one matcher.
#
# Generated by scripts/build-ds-rules.mjs from templates/ds-forms.yml.tmpl and a design-system
# facts file (design-system.example.json); edit the facts file and rebuild instead of editing this
# file. Facts read: primitivesDir, searchModule, tokens.inputBorder, components.searchInput,
# components.filterToolbar.
rules:
  - id: ds-use-text-input-primitive
    message: >-
      Plain HTML `<input>`: interactive elements are primitives, and a feature folder composes
      primitives rather than defining one. Use the text, choice, checkbox or search primitive, so
      the label, focus ring, error wiring and token ground come from one place. A file picker is
      not matched.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '**/*.test.ts'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    patterns:
      - pattern: <input ... />
      - pattern-not: <input type="file" ... />

  - id: ds-input-token-is-a-border
    message: >-
      `@@tokens.inputBorder@@` is the form-control border token and never a ground: a control that paints
      `@@tokens.inputBorder@@` behind its own text is a defect. Give the control `border: '1px solid
      var(@@tokens.inputBorder@@)'` and the control ground token as its background.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '**/*.test.ts'
    patterns:
      - pattern: '{..., $PROP: "var(@@tokens.inputBorder@@)", ...}'
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $PROP
          regex: ^(background|backgroundColor|backgroundImage)$
      - focus-metavariable: $PROP

  - id: ds-restated-field-default
    message: >-
      The text-control primitives already default `autoComplete="off"`, turn spell-check and
      auto-capitalisation off for a code control and offer a decimal pad to a number control.
      Delete the restated attribute: pass `autoComplete` only for a real token such as
      `username` or `new-password`.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    pattern-either:
      - pattern: <$C ... autoComplete="off" ... />
      - pattern: <$C ... autoCapitalize="off" ... />
      - pattern: <$C ... autoCapitalize="none" ... />
      - pattern: <$C ... type="number" ... inputMode="decimal" ... />
      - pattern: <$C ... inputMode="decimal" ... type="number" ... />

  - id: ds-hand-assembled-form-field
    message: >-
      This form field is assembled by hand: the component generates its own ids with `useId()`
      and hand-writes the `<label htmlFor=...>` that consumes them. Generating the id, binding the
      label to its control and rendering the required marker is what the field primitive does;
      use it, so the call site passes a label and a control and never a generated id.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    patterns:
      - pattern-inside: |
          const $ANYID = useId();
          ...
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: <label ... htmlFor={$X} ...>...</label>
          - pattern: <label ... htmlFor={$X} ... />

  - id: ds-no-inline-search-match
    message: >-
      Hand-written case-insensitive matching. Client-side search has exactly one matcher, which
      folds case and removes diacritics so a term matches with or without its accents; a local
      `.toLowerCase().includes(...)` is accent-blind and drifts from every other screen. Call the
      shared matcher.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.ts'
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@searchModule@@'
    patterns:
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: $H.$FOLD().$OP($Q)
          - pattern: $H.$OP($Q.$FOLD())
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $FOLD
          regex: '^(toLowerCase|toUpperCase|toLocaleLowerCase|toLocaleUpperCase)$'
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $OP
          regex: '^(includes|indexOf|lastIndexOf|startsWith|endsWith|search)$'
      # A fold-and-compare against a constant is a classifier (an error code, a language tag),
      # not a search over user input.
      - pattern-not: $H.$FOLD().$OP("...")
      - pattern-not: $H.$FOLD().$OP(`...`)
      - pattern-not: $H.$OP("...".$FOLD())

  - id: ds-no-hoisted-search-match
    message: >-
      A second search matcher: a case-folded haystack held in a local and then tested with
      `includes`/`indexOf`. This is the shared matcher rewritten by hand, without its diacritic
      normalisation. Delete the local matcher and call the shared one.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.ts'
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@searchModule@@'
    patterns:
      - pattern-inside: |
          var $H = $X.$FOLD();
          ...
      - pattern: $H.$OP($Q)
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $FOLD
          regex: '^(toLowerCase|toUpperCase|toLocaleLowerCase|toLocaleUpperCase)$'
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $OP
          regex: '^(includes|indexOf|lastIndexOf)$'
      - pattern-not: $H.$OP("...")
      - pattern-not: $H.$OP(`...`)

  - id: ds-no-hand-rolled-search-input
    message: >-
      Hand-rolled search bar. The search-input primitive has exactly one implementation: a
      leading search glyph, a clear control that appears once there is text, and the debounce
      that keeps every keystroke from reaching the search endpoint. Render the search-input
      primitive and filter with the shared matcher.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    patterns:
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: <input type="search" ... />
          - patterns:
              - pattern: <input ... $ATTR={$P} ... />
              - metavariable-regex:
                  metavariable: $ATTR
                  regex: '^(placeholder|aria-label)$'
              # Anchored at the start of the binding; `[^a-z]` under `(?i)` keeps a key such as
              # `notes.research` out.
              - metavariable-regex:
                  metavariable: $P
                  regex: '(?i)^(.*[^a-z])?search'

  - id: ds-no-duplicate-search-component
    message: >-
      `$NAME` is a second search/filter-bar component outside the primitives. The search input
      and the filter toolbar have exactly one implementation each; a feature-flavoured copy is how
      the missing clear button, the missing debounce and the accent-blind match come back one
      screen at a time. Compose the primitive instead.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    patterns:
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: 'function $NAME(...) { ... }'
          - pattern: const $NAME = ...
      - metavariable-regex:
          metavariable: $NAME
          regex: '^[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*(@@components.searchInput@@|SearchBar|SearchBox|SearchField|@@components.filterToolbar@@|FilterBar)$'

  # A list screen's search sits in the filter toolbar's `search` slot, so every list opens with
  # the same row (search, filters, count, actions) and wraps the same way. A screen whose search
  # filters no list (a command palette) is added to the excludes with its reason.
  - id: ds-search-input-outside-filter-toolbar
    message: >-
      A `@@components.searchInput@@` that is not the `search` slot of a `@@components.filterToolbar@@`. Every screen with a
      search takes the toolbar's shape, so the search sits in one row with the filters, count and
      actions. Render `<@@components.filterToolbar@@ search={<@@components.searchInput@@ ... />} />`.
    severity: ERROR
    languages:
      - typescript
    paths:
      exclude:
        - '**/*.test.tsx'
        - '@@primitivesDir@@/**'
    patterns:
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: <@@components.searchInput@@ ... />
          - pattern: <@@components.searchInput@@ ...>...</@@components.searchInput@@>
      - pattern-not-inside: <@@components.filterToolbar@@ ... search={...} ... />
